  "installation_verification_record": "setup/hillside-tram-portal/installation-verification.json",
  "included_readme": "* Hillside GLR-to-Subway Transition by morifari *\r\n\r\nThese lots can be used to simulate a GLR tunnel. Use the subway tool to connect the tunnel entrances. There are two lots included, one for more urban settings with a concrete base texture, and a rural one with a grass base texture.\r\n\r\nNote: The lots will align automatically to a network (street, road, oneway-road,...) that runs parallel to the GLR tracks. In uneven terrain, it might be necessary to level the ground a bit to ensure a proper (visual) connection between the lot and the adjacent GLR tracks.\r\n\r\nThis BAT was released on the now defunct GLR homepage by GoaSkin, so you don't need to re-download it if you have it already. For this release, I extracted the lots from the all-inclusive DAT, so you can choose what version (urban or rural) you want to install.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Compatibility *\r\n\r\nThis download is compatible with SimCity 4 Rush Hour and SimCity 4 Deluxe.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Installation *\r\n\r\nCopy all files (excluding this readme file) in \"\\My Documents\\SimCity 4\\Plugins\". It is wise to create a new folder for each download to avoid confusion.\r\n\r\nFor deinstalling the files, simply bulldoze every lot from this download in your cities and delete the files from the plugins folder afterwards.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Dependencies *\r\n\r\n- Network Addon Mod (for the GLR tracks)\r\n\r\n\r\n* Included files *\r\n\r\n- Hillside_GLR_to_subway_prop.dat\r\n- Hillside_GLR_to_subway_urban.SC4Lot\r\n- Hillside_GLR_to_subway_rural.SC4Lot\r\n\r\n\r\n* Legal stuff *\r\n\r\nThe usage of this download is on your own risk. I try to test my lots extensively, so they should work properly, but errors may still exist. I'm not responsible for any damages that may occur.\r\n\r\nFeel free to modify the lots for yourself and show them in your city journals, but please don't distribute them without asking me first.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Credits *\r\n\r\nAuthor: morifari\r\nAdditional Modding: Andreas Roth (andreas@simszone.de)"
}
